'''''Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Republic Heroes''''' is a ''Star Wars Legends'' game for [[Wikipedia:Personal computer|PC]], [[Wikipedia:Xbox 360|Xbox 360]], [[Wikipedia:PlayStation 3|PlayStation 3]], [[Wikipedia:Wii|Wii]], [[Wikipedia:PlayStation 2|PlayStation 2]], [[Wikipedia:PlayStation Portable|PlayStation Portable]], and [[Wikipedia:Nintendo DS|Nintendo DS]]. It was developed by [[Krome Studios]] and was first announced to be released on [[September 15]], [[2009]] but was then pushed back to [[October 6]].<ref name="ComicCon" /> It is based upon the [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars (film)|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' movie]] and [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|TV series]] and is set between [[The Clone Wars: Season One|Season 1]] and [[The Clone Wars: Season Two|Season 2]].

In one major difference in versions of the game, the Nintendo DS version is based on the movie, as well as episodes from Seasons 1 and 2, and serves as a prequel to the version released on other platforms.

==Plot summary==
===Nintendo DS version===
[[Obi-Wan Kenobi/Legends|Obi-Wan]], [[Cody/Legends|Cody]], [[Anakin Skywalker/Legends|Anakin]], [[Ahsoka Tano/Legends|Ahsoka]] and some [[Clone trooper/Legends|Clone troopers]] have traveled to [[Christophsis/Legends|Christophsis]] to take out a ray shield and protect their heavy cannons, while [[Kit Fisto/Legends|Kit Fisto]] has traveled to [[Grievous/Legends|Grievous]]' [[Grievous's castle/Legends|lair]] to find [[Nute Gunray/Legends|Nute Gunray]]. Ahsoka, Obi-Wan and [[Mace Windu/Legends|Mace Windu]] go to [[Ryloth/Legends|Ryloth]] to save the inhabitants from the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems/Legends|Separatists]].

[[Cad Bane/Legends|Cad Bane]] had been captured by a Droid base, and has valuable information to the [[Galactic Republic/Legends|Republic]], so Kit Fisto and [[Padmé Amidala/Legends|Padmé Amidala]] travel there to get that information.

[[R2-D2/Legends|R2-D2]] have been captured by Grievous for the Republic tactics and base locations hidden within him. On [[Skytop Station/Legends|Skytop Station]], Ahsoka, Anakin and [[Rex/Legends|Rex]] start a desperate hunt for R2. When they find him, they have to race against time to get off the falling ship. Meanwhile, [[Luminara Unduli/Legends|Luminara Unduli]] and [[Gree (clone trooper)/Legends|Gree]] return to Grievous' lair to get codes that were revealed to be hidden there by Cad Bane's information.

===Other versions===
[[Anakin Skywalker/Legends|Anakin]] and [[Ahsoka Tano/Legends|Ahsoka]] are on [[Ryloth/Legends|Ryloth]] and have to clear the way for the [[Clone trooper/Legends|Clone troopers]] by fighting through various amounts of droids. Meanwhile, the [[Juma 9]] station is under attack so [[Obi-Wan Kenobi/Legends|Obi-Wan]], [[Plo Koon/Legends|Plo Koon]], Commander [[Cody/Legends|Cody]] and [[Switch (clone trooper)|Switch]] must stop it. While going to the comms room, Obi-Wan and Plo find a [[Skakoan/Legends|Skakoan]] scientist there. They follow him, and he reveals himself to be [[Kul Teska]]. After a battle, he escapes but Obi-Wan and Plo get trapped. Since Anakin has lost contact with Obi-Wan and Plo Koon, [[Jedi Master/Legends|Jedi Masters]] [[Mace Windu/Legends|Mace Windu]] and [[Kit Fisto/Legends|Kit Fisto]] (as well as Commander [[Ponds/Legends|Ponds]]), arrive to rescue the trapped pair.

[[File:TCWRepublicHeroes-Logo.png|thumb|left|250px|Game logo]]
On [[Alzoc III/Legends|Alzoc III]], [[Aayla Secura/Legends|Aayla Secura]], [[Luminara Unduli/Legends|Luminara Unduli]], Commander [[Bly/Legends|Bly]] and Commander [[Gree (clone trooper)/Legends|Gree]] try to solve the puzzle of floating debris of a CIS ship. They discover it was destroyed by a mysterious weapon and alert the others right away. Eventually the two end up facing [[Dark Jedi/Legends|Dark Jedi]] [[Asajj Ventress/Legends|Asajj Ventress]] which was dispatched by [[Dooku/Legends|Dooku]] to get rid of any witnesses.

Back on Ryloth, Captain [[Rex/Legends|Rex]] and [[Boomer (Advanced Recon Force trooper)|Boomer]] are captured by [[Cad Bane/Legends|Cad Bane]] and told to load a [[Confederacy of Independent Systems/Legends|Separatist]] [[Gravitic polarization beam|Superweapon]] (which caused the floating debris on Alzoc III) aboard his ship, but the droids want it back. So the two clones have to stop them. Anakin and Ahsoka then come in to save the two clones but then they also have to stop the droids, too. Eventually, the five get out of the cave and Rex and Boomer decide to destroy all of the droids, leaving time for Anakin, Ahsoka, and Bane to get to his ship. When they arrive in the junkyard, they find Kul Teska.

Teska escapes so Ahsoka and Anakin contact Obi-Wan and Plo Koon only to find that Aayla, Luminara and [[Yoda/Legends|Yoda]] contacted them as well. They all find out that [[Padmé Amidala/Legends|Padmé Amidala]] has been captured by Teska, on [[Behpour/Legends|Behpour]], who has been planning with Dooku to destroy the [[Naboo/Legends|Naboo]] Star System with the superweapon. Anakin, Obi-Wan, Ahsoka, and Mace Windu go to destroy the superweapon. In the assault, Anakin and Obi-Wan sneaked into the facility to deactivate the [[Deflector shield generator/Legends|Deflector shield generator]], while Ahsoka and Mace Windu led the charge into the facility. After a fierce assault, Obi-Wan and Windu found [[Dooku/Legends|Count Dooku]] and eventually defeat him. Anakin and Ahsoka, on the other hand, fought Teska and barely escaped the facility with the rescued [[Padmé Amidala/Legends|Senator Amidala]] on two [[Single Trooper Aerial Platform/Legends|Single Trooper Aerial Platforms]].

==Gameplay==
The game allows players to play as Jedi Knights, clone troopers and other characters, and contains 40 missions. The gameplay changes on certain missions. On missions with Jedi characters, it is platforming based. On missions with clone characters, it is third-person shooter-based.
